B.Xh=new A.Am("Refund policy","Simple version: if you buy full access and are not happy, email refund@cdlfastpass.com within 7 days of purchase and we refund you in full. No forms, no argument.\n\nAfter 7 days we generally do not refund, because the product is fully available from the moment you buy. If something genuinely went wrong, for example you were charged twice or the app failed for you, email us anyway and we will make it right.\n\nRefunds go back to the card you paid with, usually within 5 to 10 business days depending on your bank. When a purchase is refunded, full access ends and your account returns to the free tier. Your study progress is never deleted.\n\nPurchases made through the Apple App Store or Google Play follow those stores' refund processes.\n",null)
B.Xi=new A.Am("Terms of service","CDL FastPass is a study tool for the commercial learner permit knowledge tests, made by OTR Drive School.\n\nWhat you get. Practice questions, exam simulators, flashcards, and video lessons. The free trial includes your first 100 questions and one exam simulator run. Full access is a one time purchase of $19.99 for your account, for the life of the product, on every platform we support.\n\nYour account. One account per person. Access is for you alone: sharing a paid account or roster seat is grounds for removing access. You are responsible for keeping your password private.\n\nWhat we promise and what we do not. We work hard to keep questions accurate against official state manuals, and we correct mistakes fast when students report them. We do not guarantee you will pass any test. Your state's DMV is the final authority on its own rules, test format, and fees, and states change these without notice.\n\nSchool roster access. If your school gave you access, that access belongs to the school arrangement and can end when it ends, for example if you leave the program.\n\nFair use. Automated scraping, bulk copying of questions, or reselling access is not allowed and will end your access without refund.\n\nLiability. To the maximum extent the law allows, our total liability to you is limited to what you paid us. We are not liable for indirect damages, or for decisions your DMV makes.\n\nChanges. If these terms change in a way that matters, we will show you the new version in the app. Continuing to use the app means you accept the change.\n\nQuestions. Email support@cdlfastpass.com and a human will answer.\n\nGoverning law: Nevada, USA.\n",null)
